### Stage 1 of the two-stage flow procedure: fit the network to the
### exact Kovasznay solution over the collocation cloud (plus the
### boundary data), with the residual weight tiny.  The result is
### fitted_weight.dat, the start of the PINN run in input_nn.dat.
Init_w       Glorot_norm
Rand_seed    20260822 /
Restart      0 /
Output_deriv 0 /

Nlayer       5 /
2 / (x, y)
40 /
40 /
40 /
3 / (u, v, p)

Loss_term  DATA         3000  colloc.dat  1.d0  /
Loss_term  DATA          480  data.dat    1.d0  /
Loss_term  COLLOCATION  3000  colloc.dat  1.d-12 /

Sys_wcomp  0.688 103.1 8.68 /   1/||y_i||^2 from the data

System 3 12 /
TRM  1  1   1 0   1.d0    /   u_x
TRM  1  2   0 1   1.d0    /   v_y
XUX  2  1 1 1 0   1.d0    /   u * u_x
XUX  2  2 1 0 1   1.d0    /   v * u_y
TRM  2  3   1 0   1.d0    /   p_x  (rho = 1)
TRM  2  1   2 0  -2.5d-2  /   -nu u_xx
TRM  2  1   0 2  -2.5d-2  /   -nu u_yy
XUX  3  1 2 1 0   1.d0    /   u * v_x
XUX  3  2 2 0 1   1.d0    /   v * v_y
TRM  3  3   0 1   1.d0    /   p_y
TRM  3  2   2 0  -2.5d-2  /   -nu v_xx
TRM  3  2   0 2  -2.5d-2  /   -nu v_yy

Hod_K      2 /
1.d0
0.d0
0.d0
Exact_solution 1 /   colloc.dat carries u*, v*, p*

Hod_dense  1 /

Hod_check  0 /
Num_validation 200 /
Validation_cyc 100 /
P_max          200000 /
Epoch      20000 /
Activation TANH /
Conv       1.d-14 /
Num_batch  100 /
Checkpoint_cyc 1000000 /
GD_method  Adam
GD_param   0.002d0 0.9d0 0.999d0 1.d-8 0.d0 /
